{"reference":"Proverbs 7","book":"Proverbs","chapter":7,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Wisdom and Folly","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The chapter’s contrast between keeping Wisdom close (vv. 1–5) and following the woman’s path toward death (vv. 6–27) participates in Proverbs 1–9’s larger portrayal of Wisdom and Folly as rival women. Their calls, homes, meals, and paths give concrete form to competing desires and to outcomes described as life or death. This reading is interpretive and remains disputed.","verse_refs":["Proverbs 7:1-27"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_proverbs_007_23534cf2e5d6cbf88f2a62d4"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}